Referring to the table for the common logarithm, we find that
\begin{aligned}\log_{10}(232\times323)&=\log_{10}[(2.32\times10^2)\times(3.23\times10^2)]\\&=\log_{10}[(2.32\times3.23)\times(10^4)]\\&=\log_{10}2.32+\log_{10}3.23+4\log_{10}10\\&=0.3655+0.5092+4\\&=0.8747+4\end{aligned}
Once again, we need to use the table in reverse:
\begin{aligned}232\times323&=10^{0.8747+4}\\&=10^{0.8747}\times10^4\\&\approx7.49\times10^4\\&=74\,900.\end{aligned}
The exact answer is 74 936. Our approximation is correct to three significant figures.

Referring to the table for the common logarithm, we find that
\begin{aligned}\log_{10}[(3.24\times10^3)^2\times(5.34\times10^4)^3]&=\log_{10}[(3.24)^2(5.34)^3(10)^{18}]\\&=2\log_{10}3.24+3\log_{10}5.34+18\log_{10}10\\&\approx2(0.5105)+3(0.7275)+18\\&=21.2035\\&=0.2035+21.\end{aligned}
As usual, we now apply the table in reverse:
\begin{aligned}(3.24\times10^3)^2\times(5.34\times10^4)^3&=10^{0.2035+21}\\&=10^{0.2035}\times10^{21}\\&\approx1.60\times10^{21}.\end{aligned}
